248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (This project addresses the growing need for efficient crowd management in public spaces such as malls, airports, and event venues by providing an automated solution for real-time people counting using video analytics. Leveraging advanced computer vision technologies like YOLOv8 for object detection and OpenCV for video processing, the system accurately detects, tracks, and counts individuals from live camera feeds. Built using Streamlit, the interactive dashboard not only visualizes real-time analytics and heatmaps but also enables zone-based monitoring, automated alerts, and easy data export. This approach overcomes the limitations of manual counting, offering a reliable, scalable, and user-friendly method to enhance safety, optimize operations, and make informed decisions in dynamic environments.)
/E (This project addresses the growing need for efficient crowd management in public spaces such as malls, airports, and event venues by providing an automated solution for real-time people counting using video analytics. Leveraging advanced computer vision technologies like YOLOv8 for object detection and OpenCV for video processing, the system accurately detects, tracks, and counts individuals from live camera feeds. Built using Streamlit, the interactive dashboard not only visualizes real-time analytics and heatmaps but also enables zone-based monitoring, automated alerts, and easy data export. This approach overcomes the limitations of manual counting, offering a reliable, scalable, and user-friendly method to enhance safety, optimize operations, and make informed decisions in dynamic environments.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
