<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (This project can be implemented in a variety of real-world public and private spaces where crowd management, safety, and operational efficiency are a concern. For example, shopping malls and retail complexes can use this system to monitor peak crowd zones, triggering alerts when specific areas like food courts or entrances become overcrowded, thereby improving customer flow and reducing safety risks. Airports, railway stations, and other transport hubs can deploy the project for real-time monitoring of waiting halls, platforms, and check-in counters, ensuring that resources are allocated dynamically and helping prevent congestion during busy hours.)
/E (This project can be implemented in a variety of real-world public and private spaces where crowd management, safety, and operational efficiency are a concern. For example, shopping malls and retail complexes can use this system to monitor peak crowd zones, triggering alerts when specific areas like food courts or entrances become overcrowded, thereby improving customer flow and reducing safety risks. Airports, railway stations, and other transport hubs can deploy the project for real-time monitoring of waiting halls, platforms, and check-in counters, ensuring that resources are allocated dynamically and helping prevent congestion during busy hours.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
